NAME
       partprobe - tell the kernel about partition table changes

SYNOPSIS
       partprobe [-s] [-d] [DEVICE...]

DESCRIPTION
       partprobe reads the partition tables of the given disks (all disks
       when none is given) and asks the kernel to update its view, so new or
       changed partitions appear in /dev and lsblk without a reboot. fdisk
       and gdisk try this when they write; when the disk is in use, the
       kernel may still have the old table, and partprobe fixes that.

OPTIONS
       -s, --summary
              Print a summary of the partitions found.

       -d, --dry-run
              Do not ask the kernel to update.

EXAMPLES
           partprobe /dev/vdb
           lsblk /dev/vdb

SEE ALSO
       partx(8), parted(8), fdisk(8), gdisk(8), udevadm(8)
